Description=
[Aquatic Survey Settings\Floating electrodes survey inversion method]
Display=Floating electrodes survey inversion
Type=Discrete
OptionsList=0,1
Default=1
User=1
Advanced=0
Description=0=use fixed water layer, 1=Incorporate water layer into the model. The 'fixed water layer' option is more suitable when the maximum thickness of the water layer is small (less than 20%) compared to the maximum depth of investigation of the survey configuration. In cases where the thickness of the water layer is significant, the 'incorporate the water layer into the model' option is more suitable. The water layer section is included into the inversion model.
Visible=1
[Aquatic Survey Settings\Resistivity variation within water layer]
Display=Resistivity variation within water layer
Type=Discrete
OptionsList=0,1
Default=1
User=1
Advanced=0
Description=0=allow resistivity to vary freely, 1=minimise resistivity variation. If the 'incorporate water layer into the model' option is selected, it is possible to minimize the resistivity variation within the water layer or to allow the water the vary freely.
Visible=1
[Aquatic Survey Settings\Water resistivity variation damping factor]
Display=Water resistivity variation damping
Type=Real
Min=0
Max=12
Default=8
User=8
Advanced=0
Description=If the 'minimize water resistivity variation' option is selected, this damping factor controls the degree which water resistivity is allowed to vary. A higher value results in a smaller resistivity variation.
Visible=1
