[Error estimates\Limit range of data weights from error estimates]
Display=Limit range of data weights
Type=Bool
Default=0
User=0
Advanced=0
Description=1=Yes, 0=No. This option is only relevant for a data set where the data error values are also given. The data error values are commonly estimated from reciprocal readings. In some cases there could be a significant error in the error estimates themselves that could lead to unusually low or high weights given to some data points. This option allows the user to set lower and upper limits on the data error weights.
Visible=1
[Error estimates\Lower limit of data weights]
Display=Lower limit of data weights
Type=Real
Min=0.2
Max=0.5
Default=0.3
User=0.3
Advanced=0
Description=It is recommended that the ratio of the upper to the lower limit is in the range of 4 to 20 times.
