[Data settings]
Selectable=0
Selected=1
DisplayName=Data
GroupName=
Advanced=0
Visible=1
Description=
[Data settings\Automatically switch electrodes for negative geometric factor]
Display=Automatically switch electrodes
Type=Bool
Default=0
User=1
Advanced=0
Description=For surface data sets with measurements given as apparent resistance, the associated apparent resistivity sometimes becomes negative due to opposite signs of geometric factor and resistance. This is often due to an electrode order where the geometric factor unintentionally is negative (e.g. C1-C2-P1-P2). When this setting is enabled, measurements with negative geometric factor have their potential electrodes (P1 and P2) switched, ensuring a positive geometric factor. When enabled, this option will enforce a positive geometric factor by switching potential electrodes, P1 and P2, when measurements with resistance and negative geometric factor are encountered. Note that this option takes effect when you load a data set.
Visible=1
[Data settings\Force resistance value to be consistant with the geometric factor]
Display=Force positive apparent resistivity
Type=Bool
Default=0
User=0
Advanced=0
Description=Under most circumstances, surface data sets should only show positive apparent resistivities. When negative resistivities are encountered, they are commonly the consequence of e.g. inconsistent sign convention for geometric factor or voltages. When this setting is enabled, apparent resistivity is forced to be positive for all measurements. Note that this option takes effect when you load a data set.
Visible=1
[Data settings\Filter input data using gemetric factor]
Display=Filter input data using geometric
Type=Bool
Default=0
User=0
Advanced=0
Description=
Visible=0
[Data settings\Automatically remove negative apparent resistivity values]
Display=Remove negative apparent resistivity
Type=Bool
Default=1
User=1
Advanced=0
Description=Under most circumstances, surface data sets should only show positive apparent resistivities. When negative resistivities are encountered, they are commonly the consequence of e.g. inconsistent sign convention for geometric factor or voltages. When this setting is enabled measurements with negative apparent resistivity are removed and never loaded into Res2DInv. Note that this option takes effect when you load a data set.
Visible=1
[Data settings\Automatically remove Gamma type arrays]
Display=Automatically remove Gamma type
Type=Bool
Default=0
User=0
Advanced=0
Description=
Visible=0
